// Rust: crates/jet-codegen/src/Prelude/CoreLib/Top/MathLibPure.rs:1480
// Decimal digit count of an Int; zero has one digit and the sign is not a
// digit. Counting on the non-positive side gives Int's minimum a magnitude.
pub fn jet_std_math_digits(value: Int) -> Int Never! {
    magnitude :: if value < 0 -> value else -> -value
    count := 1
    bound := -10
    loop magnitude <= bound {
        count += 1
        if count == 19 -> return count
        bound = bound * 10
    }
    count
}

#Test("digits counts decimal digits of every Int") {
    assert_eq(jet_std_math_digits(0), 1)
    assert_eq(jet_std_math_digits(7), 1)
    assert_eq(jet_std_math_digits(-7), 1)
    assert_eq(jet_std_math_digits(10), 2)
    assert_eq(jet_std_math_digits(-99), 2)
    assert_eq(jet_std_math_digits(1000000000000000000), 19)
    assert_eq(jet_std_math_digits(9223372036854775807), 19)
    assert_eq(jet_std_math_digits(-9223372036854775807 - 1), 19)
}
